---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SEMPODS_VERSION, SEMPODS_RELEASE_URL, implementationDoc, specificationDoc } from '../data/coordinates';
---

<Base
  title="sempods resources — contract, libraries and ways to begin"
  description="Find the development specification, Kotlin release guides, Maven artifacts, public demo and project conversations."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">the index</p>
  <h1>Find the right starting point</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The contract, the Kotlin modules and the public demonstration answer
    different questions. Here is where to go for each.
  </p>
  <h2>Understand or implement the contract</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://spec.sempods.org">Development specification</a>: normative chapters, vocabulary and optional modules.</li>
    <li><a href="https://spec.sempods.org/api/">HTTP surface</a>: the development OpenAPI descriptions rendered as a client.</li>
    <li><a href="https://schema.sempods.org">Vocabulary</a>: the project's published RDF terms.</li>
    <li><a href={specificationDoc('GOVERNANCE.md')}>Governance</a>: adoption, independent versions and identifier guarantees.</li>
    <li><a href={specificationDoc('docs/guides/specification-revisions.md')}>Choose a revision</a>: obtain a consistent source snapshot.</li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/sempods/sempods-spec">sempods-spec repository</a>: chapters, OpenAPI, vocabulary and proposals.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Use Kotlin {SEMPODS_VERSION}</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={SEMPODS_RELEASE_URL}>Release notes</a>: what changed and known limitations.</li>
    <li><a href={implementationDoc('sempods-client/README.md')}>JVM client guide</a>: module choice and tested examples.</li>
    <li><a href={implementationDoc('docs/migration/0.2.md')}>Migration from 0.1</a>: client and operator changes.</li>
    <li><a href={implementationDoc('docs/concepts/modularity.md')}>Modularity and deployment</a>: select components and understand upgrade responsibility.</li>
    <li><a href="https://central.sonatype.com/namespace/org.sempods">Maven Central</a>: published artifacts. See <a href="/start#build">Start</a> for runtime requirements and coordinates.</li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/sempods/sempods-kotlin">sempods-kotlin repository</a>: reusable services, libraries and the reference composition.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Try the model</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/start#query">Query a public pod</a>: live aaltra event data, no account needed.</li>
    <li><a href="https://apps.sempods.org/explorer/">Explorer preview</a>: browse resources and links in an experimental app.</li>
    <li><a href="/start#run">Run the development composition</a>: a tagged starting point for your own setup.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Talk or contribute</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/sempods/sempods-kotlin/discussions">Discussions</a>: questions and ideas for the project.</li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/sempods/sempods-kotlin/issues">Implementation issues</a> and <a href="https://github.com/sempods/sempods-spec/issues">specification issues</a>: report a problem in the responsible repository.</li>
    <li><a href="mailto:hello@sempods.org">hello@sempods.org</a>: private questions or a test-pod request.</li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/sempods/sempods-website">Website source</a> and <a href="https://github.com/sempods">sempods organisation</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="action-links">
    <a href="/start">Choose your path</a>{' '}
    <a href="/how-it-works">Understand the model</a>
  </p>
</Base>
